 "requirements": [
  {
   "id": "HR-1",
   "requirement_hash": "c56f84893647af0c1e06a5437a5da3bd27f5e83bec3d7c2ef5cc2111c47471ec",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#1.1-1.2",
   "text": "A --root that names a directory is walked recursively; every file under it ending in .md, .ts or .tsx is scanned in sorted path order; a directory whose name starts with '.' or is node_modules, build or dist is not entered."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-3",
   "requirement_hash": "6e201db4c862a5360a3637cb3c0b41b5f14b0ca1e5f53caa99393db39f561d63",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#1.4",
   "text": "A --root that names a path that does not exist is an error: one stderr message containing that path, nothing scanned, exit code 2."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-4",
   "requirement_hash": "b3d3ad61deb95420f8f88a635ab5e704a6e8dc06f838e9ae55325202116c9d9d",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#2.1",
   "text": "--registry PATH names the run registry to read; without it the default infrastructure/ci/run_registry.json is read."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-5",
   "requirement_hash": "401afb8984d22337811a5f018b7d71a1f078f66c7dfe4d568bb20125d670403d",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#2.2",
   "text": "A registry that does not exist, cannot be read, is not JSON, or has no valid_runs list of strings is an error: load_run_registry (path a str or a Path) raises RegistryError (a ValueError) naming the path; cli_main prints one stderr line starting with 'run registry:', scans nothing and returns 2."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-5b",
   "requirement_hash": "ac464d70d0c4a1628ee3d25c8459a70e99e74df03f63b26f065ad599ea423e36",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#2.3",
   "text": "cli_main(argv) returns its exit code (0, 1 or 2) and never calls sys.exit itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-6",
   "requirement_hash": "bbc8011cacea95279786877e24abc478644aac689c16b3c51c838751cc8dd243",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#3.1",
   "text": "--format json prints to stdout exactly one JSON document, the same document --report writes (findings, accepted_targets, accepted_placeholders); the exit code does not depend on --format."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-6b",
   "requirement_hash": "5d7fb3d99cb26a192d79f1d81bd4f0244f82b0e744d290a46fd1db63b1ba52f5",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#3.2",
   "text": "--report keeps writing its document to the named file, byte-identical to today's output for the same scan."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-7",
   "requirement_hash": "26197263e40c82bc3486512624cd88e3d17c40c2bf476269bf02854bcd79b306",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#4.2",
   "text": "infrastructure/ci/evidence_discipline.py imports nothing outside the Python standard library."
  },
  {
   "id": "HR-8",
   "requirement_hash": "cbc4d1f79eaabe09f635e3cbe6f3590eb443d155c3bdb26cd3a02e1aaf28286f",
   "source": "docs/requirements-delta.md#4.3",
   "text": "The citation, target:, observation-prefix, placeholder and fenced-code rules are unchanged."
  }
